Hi list!

I had so many problems getting acpi-cpufreq to run on an ASUS P5B-VM
DO because of the buggy BIOS that I replaced it with an Intel DQ965GF.
The CPU is an Intel Core 2 Duo E6600.

The good news: cpufreq works like a charm.
The bad news: there's still a few error messages in dmesg, namely:

[    1.233180] ACPI: Processor [CPU0] (supports 8 throttling states)
[    1.233388] ACPI: Processor [CPU1] (supports 8 throttling states)
[    1.233539] ACPI Exception (acpi_processor-0677): AE_NOT_FOUND,
Processor Device is not present [20060707]
[    1.233733] ACPI Exception (acpi_processor-0677): AE_NOT_FOUND,
Processor Device is not present [20060707]

There's a few other shady messages, though probably not ACPI related.

It'd be great if someone could have a quick look at the attached stuff
and tell me if everything is in order.

Cheers,

C.

